# Repository context (applies to all work in this repo)

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before writing or editing code.** It is the
tool-agnostic source of truth for this repository — architecture, the page-object
schema, validation invariants, build outputs, JS/CSS idioms, testing, and
commit/PR conventions.

This file is deliberately a pointer and nothing more. It used to restate a
summary of the architecture, and that summary rotted: it went on describing
hand-maintained `<script>` tags and "no bundler, no ES modules" for months after
the Vite migration removed both, and quoted a unit-test-file count less than half
the real one. A mirror that repeats facts drifts from them; a mirror that points
at them cannot.

It also carried a verbatim copy of a third-party "design-only workflow" that had
nothing to do with this repository — it directed agents to build with Tailwind and
Flowbite, pick Google Fonts, put `!important` on everything, and avoid blue. This
project uses `@sfgov/design-system` with `--sfds-*` design tokens, reserves
`!important` for one designated override layer, and is built around SF.gov's blue
brand palette. For design work, read the CSS section of `AGENTS.md` and the token
layer in `css/theme.css`.

If you need a fact about this repo, get it from `AGENTS.md`. If `AGENTS.md` is
missing something you had to work out for yourself, add it there.
